<caml:Content xmlns:caml="http://lc.ca.gov/legalservices/schemas/caml.1#"><p>Notwithstanding any other provision of law, a person or entity may not do any of the following:</p><p>(a)<span class="EnSpace"/>Initiate or advertise in an unsolicited commercial e-mail advertisement from California or advertise in an unsolicited commercial e-mail advertisement sent from California.</p><p>(b)<span class="EnSpace"/>Initiate or advertise in an unsolicited commercial e-mail advertisement to a California electronic mail address, or advertise in an unsolicited commercial e-mail
				  advertisement sent to a California electronic mail address.</p><p>(c)<span class="EnSpace"/>The provisions of this section are severable. If any provision of this section or its application is held invalid, that invalidity shall not affect any other provision or application that can be given effect without the invalid provision or application.</p></caml:Content>